# Build context exclusions.
#
# Note what is NOT excluded: apps/ and tests/. The service Dockerfiles copy
# every workspace manifest before installing, because `npm ci` validates the
# lockfile against the full workspace graph and fails on a missing package.json
# even for a workspace the service never imports. Excluding those directories
# wholesale would break the COPY that needs them.
#
# So the heavy contents are excluded instead of the directories.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# Foundry artifacts. Rebuilt from source, and out/ alone is tens of megabytes.
cache
out
lib
broadcast

.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Application source the services do not run. The manifests are still copied
# explicitly by the Dockerfiles; only the code and assets are skipped.
apps/*/app
apps/*/components
apps/*/hooks
apps/*/lib
apps/*/styles
apps/*/public

docs
scripts
infra/monitoring
**/*.md
**/*.log
